            "text": "An optimized solution that resolves the kernel OOM issue. \n\n### Why the Previous Run Failed\nBroadcasting all pairs over 1024 dimensions (`vectors[:, None, :] - vectors[None, :, :]`) attempts to materialize an $8000 \\times 8000 \\times 1024$ `float32` array requiring $\\approx 262\\text{ GB}$ of RAM, triggering an immediate kernel OOM kill (exit code -9).\n\n### Strategy\n1. Promote the data to `float64` to avoid catastrophic cancellation in distance calculations.\n2. Use the algebraic identity $\\|u - v\\|^2 = \\|u\\|^2 + \\|v\\|^2 - 2\\langle u, v \\rangle$, computing the cross terms via multi-threaded BLAS matrix multiplication.\n3. Process rows in blocks of 1,000 to keep the peak working memory below 200 MB while completing computation in around 1 second.\n4. Explicitly zero out diagonal entries and clamp any tiny negative values caused by floating-point rounding before computing square roots.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load vectors in read-only mode to prevent any modification\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy', mmap_mode='r')\n    \n    # Cast to float64 for numerical precision\n    X_64 = X.astype(np.float64)\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X_64 ** 2, axis=1)\n    \n    N = len(X_64)\n    chunk_size = 1000\n    total_distance = 0.0\n    \n    for i in range(0, N, chunk_size):\n        chunk = X_64[i:i + chunk_size]\n        \n        # ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2 <u, v>\n        # Shape: (len(chunk), N)\n        dists_sq = sq_norms[i:i + len(chunk), None] + sq_norms[None, :] - 2.0 * (chunk @ X_64.T)\n        \n        # Explicitly set diagonal to zero\n        row_idx = np.arange(len(chunk))\n        col_idx = i + row_idx\n        dists_sq[row_idx, col_idx] = 0.0\n        \n        # Clamp negative values caused by floating-point inaccuracies\n        np.maximum(dists_sq, 0.0, out=dists_sq)\n        \n        total_distance += float(np.sqrt(dists_sq, out=dists_sq).sum())\n        \n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total_distance}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
